        ("Repairs that fit a carefully kept village",
         "Once the colony is out, there is usually an opening to close: a cut in stucco, a lifted roof tile, a panel off a soffit. Our own licensed contractors, roofers and painters do that work, so one company opens the hole, closes it and stands behind it. Our workmanship carries a warranty: should a colony try that same sealed gap again, a crew returns.\n\nThe village runs its own Building Department and an architectural board, so before any change visible from the street, ask Village Hall whether the patch needs a permit or sign-off. A like-for-like repair is the usual goal. The [[svc:repairs|repairs after removal]] page lists what can be rebuilt, and the [[page:cost|cost page]] explains why a job with repairs runs well past a simple ground-level removal."),
